# CODEOWNERS — normative-surface backstop (CONTRACT-GUARD-1).
#
# These paths are FLAG-AND-WAIT per the workspace escalation policy
# (../CLAUDE.md). Tim owns them so a PR touching any of them requires his
# review — the merge-time backstop to scripts/check-protected-paths.mjs's
# pre-push gate. This enforces at MERGE, not at commit: it cannot stop a
# session from proposing the change, only from merging it unreviewed. For it
# to bite, "Require review from Code Owners" must be enabled in branch
# protection on this repo.
#
# The last three rows (GUARD-SELF-1) protect the enforcement machinery
# itself — listing a path in the workflow's `paths:` trigger only makes it
# TRIGGER; only PROTECTED_PATHS + CODEOWNERS make it PROTECTED.

/CONTRACT.md                                       @collectrix
/chaingraph/standard/SPEC.md                        @collectrix
/chaingraph/standard/openchain-graph-v0.4.schema.json @collectrix
/.github/workflows/protected-paths.yml             @collectrix
/scripts/check-protected-paths.mjs                 @collectrix
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                @collectrix
